1248:
The administrative officer has the power and duty to provide the following services related to these regulations:
(a) Provide initial information about these regulations upon request;
(b) Advise how to contact members of the planning commission, the board of appeals, and the Lamar County Board of Commissioners for services provided by those bodies;
(c) Offer practical suggestions on how to comply with the requirements of these regulations;
(d) Maintain complete records concerning these regulations and related matters, and make such records available to the public upon request;
(e) Propose amendments to these regulations.
(Ord. of 3-6-01)

1249:
The planning commission has the power and duty to provide the following services related to these regulations:
(a) Advise the Lamar County Board of Commissioners on applications for amendment to these regulations by examining amendment applications and providing written recommendations with reasons for the recommendations to the Lamar County Board of Commissioners as specified in section 410 of the zoning ordinance;
(b) Dispense general information about these regulations to the public upon request;
(c) Propose amendments to these regulations;
(d) Carry out an ongoing comprehensive planning program, which like the land use plan, will provide current data on which decisions regarding these regulations may be based that utilize sound planning principles.
(Ord. of 3-6-01)

1250:
The board of appeals has the power and duty to provide the following services:
(a) Accept applications for appeal of an action of the administrative officer or the planning commission and render official decisions on them according to procedures specified in section 406 of the zoning ordinance;
(b) Recommend approval or denial of special exceptions required for the construction and installation of towers and/or antennas in accordance with article 5 of these regulations;
(c) Authorize variances according to procedures specified in section 407 of the zoning ordinance.
(Ord. of 3-6-01)

1251:
The board of commissioners has the power and duty to provide the following services to these regulations:
(a) Approve or deny special exceptions required for the construction and installation of towers and/or antennas;
(b) Accept applications for amendment of these regulations and render official decisions on them after referring them to the planning commission for review and recommendations as specified in section 410 of the zoning ordinance;
(c) Propose amendments to these regulations.
(Ord. of 3-6-01)
